    "Regularity" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Regularity"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Regularidad"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Regularity is how much your mid-sleep point moves night to night (the midpoint between falling asleep and waking): it predicts your health better than total hours. Naps don't count. \"Need\" is the 7–9 h target, not a measurement of you." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Regularity is how much your mid-sleep point moves night to night (the midpoint between falling asleep and waking): it predicts your health better than total hours. Naps don't count. \"Need\" is the 7–9 h target, not a measurement of you."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La regularidad es qué tanto se mueve tu punto medio de sueño (el punto entre dormirte y despertar) noche a noche: predice tu salud mejor que las horas totales. Las siestas no cuentan. «Necesidad» es la meta 7–9 h, no una medición tuya."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Regularity is the night-to-night variability of your mid-sleep point (the midpoint between falling asleep and waking): a steadier schedule predicts health more strongly than how long you sleep. Naps don't count: only your main night (at least 3 h) feeds regularity. Stages are estimated from movement, heart rate and HRV, so they're approximate; deep sleep repairs the body, REM consolidates memory and emotion. \"Need\" is a 7–9 h population target, not a measurement of you." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Regularity is the night-to-night variability of your mid-sleep point (the midpoint between falling asleep and waking): a steadier schedule predicts health more strongly than how long you sleep. Naps don't count: only your main night (at least 3 h) feeds regularity. Stages are estimated from movement, heart rate and HRV, so they're approximate; deep sleep repairs the body, REM consolidates memory and emotion. \"Need\" is a 7–9 h population target, not a measurement of you."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La regularidad es la variabilidad noche a noche de tu punto medio de sueño (el punto medio entre dormirte y despertar): un horario más estable predice la salud con más fuerza que cuántas horas duermes. Las siestas no cuentan: solo tu noche principal (al menos 3 h) alimenta la regularidad. Las etapas se estiman con movimiento, ritmo cardiaco y VFC, así que son aproximadas; el sueño profundo repara el cuerpo, el REM consolida memoria y emoción. La «necesidad» es una meta poblacional de 7 a 9 h, no una medición de ti."
          }
        }
      }
    },
