    "The number is the most recent calculated value; the chart traces the daily values across the range." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The number is the most recent calculated value; the chart traces the daily values across the range."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El número es el valor calculado más reciente; la gráfica traza los diarios del rango."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The number is the most recent value in this series; the chart traces the daily values across the range." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The number is the most recent value in this series; the chart traces the daily values across the range."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El número es el valor más reciente de esta serie; la gráfica traza los diarios del rango."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The number you see is the HRV Apple records: SDNN, the overall spread of the time between your heartbeats. Your daily verdict does NOT read this signal (SDNN): it stands on your resting heart rate and your sleep, and on your nocturnal RMSSD when the night is dense enough. SDNN is shown here as a reference against your own average. The trend uses a different HRV measure, RMSSD, recomputed from the beat-to-beat intervals of your densest nights; RMSSD tracks the vagal, rest-and-repair branch specifically, while SDNN blends both branches, so the two won't always move together." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The number you see is the HRV Apple records: SDNN, the overall spread of the time between your heartbeats. Your daily verdict does NOT read this signal (SDNN): it stands on your resting heart rate and your sleep, and on your nocturnal RMSSD when the night is dense enough. SDNN is shown here as a reference against your own average. The trend uses a different HRV measure, RMSSD, recomputed from the beat-to-beat intervals of your densest nights; RMSSD tracks the vagal, rest-and-repair branch specifically, while SDNN blends both branches, so the two won't always move together."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El número que ves es la VFC que registra Apple: SDNN, la dispersión general del tiempo entre tus latidos. Tu veredicto diario NO lee esta señal (SDNN): se apoya en tu FC en reposo y en tu sueño, y en tu RMSSD nocturna cuando la noche trae suficientes latidos. El SDNN se muestra aquí como referencia contra tu propio promedio. La tendencia usa otra medida de VFC, RMSSD, recalculada desde los intervalos latido a latido de tus noches más densas; RMSSD sigue específicamente a la rama vagal, de descanso y reparación, mientras que SDNN mezcla las dos ramas, así que no siempre se mueven juntas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The number you see is the HRV Apple records: SDNN, the overall spread of the time between your heartbeats. Your daily verdict does NOT read this signal: it stands on your resting heart rate and your sleep. HRV is shown here as a reference against your own average. The trend uses a different HRV measure, RMSSD, recomputed from the beat-to-beat intervals of your densest nights; RMSSD tracks the vagal, rest-and-repair branch specifically, while SDNN blends both branches, so the two won't always move together." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The number you see is the HRV Apple records: SDNN, the overall spread of the time between your heartbeats. Your daily verdict does NOT read this signal: it stands on your resting heart rate and your sleep. HRV is shown here as a reference against your own average. The trend uses a different HRV measure, RMSSD, recomputed from the beat-to-beat intervals of your densest nights; RMSSD tracks the vagal, rest-and-repair branch specifically, while SDNN blends both branches, so the two won't always move together."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El número que ves es la VFC que registra Apple: SDNN, la dispersión general del tiempo entre tus latidos. Tu veredicto diario NO lee esta señal: se apoya en tu FC en reposo y en tu sueño. La VFC se muestra aquí como referencia contra tu propio promedio. La tendencia usa otra medida de VFC, RMSSD, recalculada desde los intervalos latido a latido de tus noches más densas; RMSSD sigue específicamente a la rama vagal, de descanso y reparación, mientras que SDNN mezcla las dos ramas, así que no siempre se mueven juntas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The only notice that survives locking your phone: a notification your iPhone delivers on its own, for when you leave it on the floor between sets. It's scheduled and delivered on your device; nothing leaves it." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El único aviso que sobrevive a que bloquees el teléfono: una notificación que tu iPhone entrega por su cuenta, para cuando lo dejas en el piso entre series. Se programa y se entrega en tu dispositivo; nada sale de ahí."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The orb is still asleep" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El orbe aún duerme"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The oxygen in your blood, read at your wrist while you sleep. A healthy adult usually stays at 95% or above." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The oxygen in your blood, read at your wrist while you sleep. A healthy adult usually stays at 95% or above."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El oxígeno en tu sangre, medido en la muñeca mientras duermes. Un adulto sano suele mantenerse en 95% o más."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The phase is estimated from the wrist temperature your Apple Watch measures while you sleep. It takes a Series 8, Ultra or newer, worn to bed every night, and about 5 nights before Apple starts giving me a reading. Once those nights land, I'll pick the estimate back up." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La fase se estima con la temperatura de muñeca que mide tu Apple Watch mientras duermes. Necesita un Series 8, Ultra o más nuevo, puesto para dormir cada noche, y unas 5 noches antes de que Apple empiece a darme una lectura. En cuanto lleguen esas noches, retomo la estimación."
          }
        }
      }
    },
