    "Your Apple Watch estimates VO₂max during outdoor walks and runs with a good GPS signal." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Apple Watch estimates VO₂max during outdoor walks and runs with a good GPS signal."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tu Apple Watch estima el VO₂max en caminatas y carreras al aire libre con buena señal de GPS."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your Apple Watch estimates VO₂max from your heart rate and pace during brisk outdoor walks and runs with a good GPS signal, so it updates every so often rather than daily. We read where it sits among healthy adults of your age and sex (the FRIEND reference median), and translate that into a plain band. A higher VO₂max is associated with a lower risk of all-cause mortality: it's one of the best-evidenced markers of long-term health." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Apple Watch estimates VO₂max from your heart rate and pace during brisk outdoor walks and runs with a good GPS signal, so it updates every so often rather than daily. We read where it sits among healthy adults of your age and sex (the FRIEND reference median), and translate that into a plain band. A higher VO₂max is associated with a lower risk of all-cause mortality: it's one of the best-evidenced markers of long-term health."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tu Apple Watch estima el VO₂max a partir de tu frecuencia cardiaca y tu ritmo en caminatas y carreras al aire libre con buena señal de GPS, así que se actualiza de vez en cuando, no a diario. Leemos dónde cae entre adultos sanos de tu edad y sexo (la mediana de referencia FRIEND) y lo traducimos en una banda sencilla. Un VO₂max más alto se asocia con menor riesgo de mortalidad por todas las causas, es uno de los marcadores de salud a largo plazo mejor fundamentados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your Apple Watch reads your skin temperature through the night; Cénit averages the worn, asleep portion and compares it with your own recent baseline, so what you see is the deviation in °C, not a raw temperature. Around your base is normal; a sustained rise of roughly +0.4 °C or more is a classic early illness marker, so Cénit flags it as running warm (~+0.4 °C) or well above (~+0.8 °C)." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Apple Watch reads your skin temperature through the night; Cénit averages the worn, asleep portion and compares it with your own recent baseline, so what you see is the deviation in °C, not a raw temperature. Around your base is normal; a sustained rise of roughly +0.4 °C or more is a classic early illness marker, so Cénit flags it as running warm (~+0.4 °C) or well above (~+0.8 °C)."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tu Apple Watch lee la temperatura de tu piel durante la noche; Cénit promedia la parte con el reloj puesto y dormido, y la compara con tu propia base reciente, así que lo que ves es la desviación en °C, no una temperatura cruda. Cerca de tu base es normal; una subida sostenida de alrededor de +0.4 °C o más es un marcador clásico de enfermedad temprana, así que Cénit la marca como corriendo caliente (~+0.4 °C) o muy por encima (~+0.8 °C)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your Apple Watch's estimate of your aerobic fitness: how well your body uses oxygen. Higher usually means better cardio shape; it's an estimate, not a lab test." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Apple Watch's estimate of your aerobic fitness: how well your body uses oxygen. Higher usually means better cardio shape; it's an estimate, not a lab test."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La estimación que hace tu Apple Watch de tu condición aeróbica: qué tan bien usa tu cuerpo el oxígeno. Más alto suele significar mejor forma cardiovascular; es una estimación, no una prueba de laboratorio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your HRV by frequency" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
