    "Your resting heart rate against your own base is the vote: Apple's densest, most reliable signal, so it carries this axis on its own." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your resting heart rate against your own base is the vote: Apple's densest, most reliable signal, so it carries this axis on its own."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tu pulso en reposo contra tu propia base es el voto: la señal más densa y confiable de Apple, así carga este eje por sí sola."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your resting heart rate is how hard your heart works when your body is fully at rest. Fitter people tend to have a lower one, though age, genetics, and some medications shape it too. Cénit reads it against your own norm as part of your daily verdict: a rise above your usual tends to show up when you're run down, short on sleep, or fighting something off. On its own it's a noisy signal, so it counts most alongside your other signs." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your resting heart rate is how hard your heart works when your body is fully at rest. Fitter people tend to have a lower one, though age, genetics, and some medications shape it too. Cénit reads it against your own norm as part of your daily verdict: a rise above your usual tends to show up when you're run down, short on sleep, or fighting something off. On its own it's a noisy signal, so it counts most alongside your other signs."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tu frecuencia cardiaca en reposo es qué tanto trabaja tu corazón cuando tu cuerpo está en completo reposo. Quien está en mejor forma suele tenerla más baja, aunque también influyen la edad, la genética y algunos medicamentos. Cénit la compara con tu propia norma como parte de tu veredicto del día: una subida por encima de lo habitual suele aparecer cuando el cuerpo viene cansado, dormiste mal o está peleando algo. Por sí sola es una señal ruidosa, así que pesa más junto con tus demás señales."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your resting heart rate woke up above your base." : {
